on on interacting includes reasoning. For example, the section on interacting includes reasoning. A discussion on how more complex methods can be developed using reasoning is given in Section 1.1 and Section 2.4.\\n\\n   We discuss the following methods for multi-step reasoning:\\n\\n   This section reviews the literature that uses multi-step reasoning to improve their problem-solving skills. This\\n   section discusses various methods for multi-step reasoning, and methods for self-reflection and retrieval\\n   augmentation. We note that the search methods and the topic also extend beyond the section. For example, the\\n   section on interacting includes reasoning. For example, the section on interacting includes reasoning. A discussion on how more complex methods can be developed using reasoning is given in Section 1.1 and Section 2.4.\\n\\n   We discuss the following methods for multi-step reasoning:\\n\\n   This section reviews the literature that uses multi-step reasoning to improve their problem-solving skills. This\\n   section discusses various methods for multi-step reasoning, and methods for self-reflection and retrieval\\n   augmentation. We note that the search methods and the topic also extend beyond the section. For example, the\\n   section on interacting includes reasoning. For example, the section on interacting includes reasoning. A discussion on how more complex methods can be developed using reasoning is given in Section 1.1 and Section 2.4.\\n\\n   We discuss the following methods for multi-step reasoning:\\n\\n   This section reviews the literature that uses multi-step reasoning to improve their problem-solving skills. This\\n   section discusses various methods for multi-step reasoning, and methods for self-reflection and retrieval\\n   augmentation. We note that the search methods and the topic also extend beyond the section. For example, the\\n   section on interacting includes reasoning. For example, the section on interacting includes reasoning. A discussion on how more complex methods can be developed using reasoning is given in Section 1.1 and Section 2.4.\\n\\n   We discuss the following methods for multi-step reasoning:\\n\\n   This section reviews the literature that uses multi-step reasoning to improve their problem-solving skills. This\\n   section discusses various methods for multi-step reasoning, and methods for self-reflection and retrieval\\n   augmentation. We note that the search methods and the topic also extend beyond the section. For example, the\\n   section on interacting includes reasoning. For example, the section on interacting includes reasoning. A discussion on how more complex methods can be developed using reasoning is given in Section 1.1 and Section 2.4.\\n\\n   We discuss the following methods for multi-step reasoning:\\n\\n   This section reviews the literature that uses multi-step reasoning to improve their problem-solving skills. This\\n   section discusses various methods for multi-step reasoning, and methods for self-reflection and retrieval\\n   augmentation. We note that the search methods and the topic also extend beyond the section. For example, the\\n   section on interacting includes reasoning. For example, the section on interacting includes reasoning. A discussion on how more complex methods can be developed using reasoning is given in Section 1.1 and Section 2.4.\\n\\n   We discuss the following methods for multi-step reasoning:\\n\\n   This section reviews the literature that uses multi-step reasoning to improve their problem-solving skills. This\\n   section discusses various methods for multi-step reasoning, and methods for self-reflection and retrieval\\n   augmentation. We note that the search methods and the topic also extend beyond the section. For example, the\\n   section on interacting includes reasoning. For example, the section on interacting includes reasoning. A discussion on how more complex methods can be developed using reasoning is given in Section 1.1 and Section 2.4.\\n\\n   We discuss the following methods for multi-step reasoning:\\n\\n   This section reviews the literature that uses multi-step reasoning to improve their problem-solving skills. This\\n   section discusses various methods for multi-step reasoning, and methods for self-reflection and retrieval\\n   augmentation. We note that the search methods and the topic also extend beyond the section. For example, the\\n   section on interacting includes reasoning. For example, the section on interacting includes reasoning. A discussion on how more complex methods can be developed using reasoning is given in Section 1.1 and Section 2.4.\\n\\n   We discuss the following methods for multi-step reasoning:\\n\\n   This section reviews the literature that uses multi-step reasoning to improve their problem-solving skills. This\\n   section discusses various methods for multi-step reasoning, and methods for self-reflection and retrieval\\n   augmentation. We note that the search methods and the topic also extend beyond the section. For example, the\\n   section on interacting includes reasoning. For example, the section on interacting includes reasoning.", "reasoning_content": "We need continue. Need read pages 9-52 in batches via read_pdf, form notes. Already pages 1-8 exposed. Need ensure 52 pages read. We have 29 model calls. Need be efficient. Each request <=32k chars including notes eventually. read_pdf tool per call likely content into evidence; can read batches. We need notes topics. Need answer exact questions.\n\nLet's read pages 9-16 batch, 17-24, etc. But full text 44 pages maybe ~150k chars, must batch. read_pdf returns JSON; probably each page ~3-4k chars. 8 pages ~30k plus overhead too much perhaps request body limit includes tool result? Model request with content? Evidence inserted likely. Need batches of 6 pages (~22k) safe. 44 pages => 8 calls. We have 29 calls. Then notes 5 (maybe grouped? save_note each call) and final report. Need p