soning/tool_use maybe.\nCall B: pages 21-26.\nCall C: pages 27-32.\nCall D: pages 33-38.\nCall E: pages 39-44.\nCall F: pages 45-52 (8 pages, but some are references; page 52 end).\n\nThat's 6 calls plus get_evidence for 9,10,13 etc. I already have 9,10,12,13,14 content in this request. Page 11, 12, 13, 14 exposed.\n\nWait page 13 content I haven't seen in this request (only catalog). But page 12 in request mentions search tree starting. Page 13 has ToT.\n\nLet me first read 13 and 15-19 together? read_pdf(max pages) - I can do multiple read_pdf calls but each returns content into the request. 7 pages * ~4000 = 28000 chars, plus prompt overhead ~ the system prompt is large. Risky. Let's do 5 pages per call: ~20k chars.\n\nLet me do read_pdf(13,17) = 5 pages.\n\nActually I should be efficient with calls. ~27 remaining. Need: 5 reads batches (15-52 = 38 pages, at 6 pages/call = 7 calls), 5 notes, 1-2 report writes, 1 pytest. That's ~15. Fine.\n\nLet me start with read_pdf(13,18).\n\nActually I already have 14. Let me read 13,15,16,17,18 — but read_pdf takes contiguous range; 13-18 includes 14 (dup, fine, 6 pages ~24k). Hmm, risk of overflow with big system prompt. Let me do 13-17 (5 pages).\n\nI'll avoid including duplicate content. Let's do 13-17.\n\nFirst, maybe save notes for overview and reasoning from what I have. But I need page 2 for overview search methods; I have pages 1,2,3 in catalog but not in this request content. Actually ev-000014 page 1, ev-000015 page 2, ev-000016 page 3 are exposed=true meaning they were in earlier requests, not this one. I need to recall them with get_evidence to write accurate notes... but re-reading costs requests. get_evidence pins it in next request — that costs a call too.\n\nHmm. I can read_pdf(1,3) again cheaply? That re-extracts. But those pages were already extracted (recorded). Re-reading duplicates but ensures I see text. 3 pages ~13k chars. Combined with 13-17 would be too much.\n\nPlan:\nCall 1: read_pdf(13,16) — 4 page