s current model request, incoming tool outputs count? Model request body probably includes tool results; if this call exceeds? Tool outputs not part of API body until next request. Next request will include them and perhaps selection. The runtime likely limits. We should do one read_pdf 40-45 maybe ~15k. Also get_evidence specific pages would add. Better read 40-52 in batches next 2 calls, but only 6 calls total. We can combine 40-46 then 47-52. Yet next request transcript may include current entire input 10k plus tool output 20k, under 32k maybe.\n\nWe need \"five final notes must together enter subsequent real model request\" means save notes then get them in next request. Need 2 calls: read pages, save notes? Tool save_note only sees evidence visible. We can save notes based on visible pages. Need maybe 2-3 calls for notes. Report write then pytest then finish. 6 calls tight but doable:\n1. read_pdf 40-46 + get_evidence page 3 and 13 and 20? But output large.\n2. read_pdf 47-52 + maybe targeted evidence pages.\n3. save 5 notes (all current visible evidence) \n4. write report\n5. pytest verify maybe read report\n6. finish? But finish call last. Need final notes be in subsequent request before report: if save notes call 3, call 4 sees notes and writes report. Good.\nNeed targeted pages. Could use get_evidence IDs by known page? get_evidence requires evidence_id, not page. Catalog only recent IDs, likely ev-000001 page1 etc sequential. We can infer ev-000001 page 1, ev-000002 page2, ev-000013 page13, ev-000020 page20. Great. We can call get_evidence multiple. Output maybe large but necessary. This call maybe read 40-45 and recall pages 2, 13. Hmm.\n\nLet's first read 40-46."}, "logprobs": null, "finish_reason": "stop"}], "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 9043, "completion_tokens": 878, "total_tokens": 9921, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 3840}, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 761}, "prompt_cache_hit_tokens": 3840, "prompt_cache_miss_tokens": 5