s? likely \"reasoning\", \"acting\", \"interacting\"? The paper Agentic LLM survey divides into reasoning, tool use, multi-agent? Prompt's five themes: overview, reasoning, tool_use, multi_agent, outlook. Table likely capabilities: reasoning, acting, interacting? Need exact.\n- search methods: initial keyword search then snowballing? \"forward and backward snowballing\"? Need answer.\n- Self Consistency: majority voting over reasoning paths.\n- ToT search controllers: BFS and DFS.\n- Toolformer tools five: calculator, calendar, machine translation, question answering, web search? Possibly calculator, question answering, machine translation, web search, Wikipedia search. Need exact.\n- ToolBench API count: 16,464? ToolBench includes 16,464 APIs? I recall ToolBench: \"16,464 RESTful APIs across 49 categories\" maybe.\n- CAMEL inception prompting.\n- Generative agents evaluators: 100? Human evaluators? likely 100.\n- Table 4 five agenda topics: \"reasoning\", \"tool use\", \"multi-agent\", \"safety\", \"evaluation\"? Need exact.\n- shared foundations: \"reasoning\" and \"memory\"? The conclusion says all three abilities benefit from \"reasoning\" and \"memory\"? Let's recall paper. Agentic LLM survey by Plaat et al. Taxonomy: \"reasoning\", \"acting\", \"interacting\" maybe. Abstract: \"We discuss three main categories: (1) LLMs as reasoners, (2) LLMs as tool users, and (3) LLMs as agents that interact with each other.\" Or \"reasoning, acting, interacting\" (three abilities). Table 4 research agenda topics perhaps \"Reasoning\", \"Memory\", \"Tool use\", \"Multi-agent\", \"Safety\"? Shared foundations maybe \"reasoning and memory\"? Need read pages 48-52.\n\nWe have 4 calls. Need plan reading 40-52 and report. Can maybe compress by fetching pages 46-52 first since likely agenda. Page 40-45 multi-agent details but already pages 37-39. Requirement read all though. Could combine pages 40-52 in 2 calls with 7 and 6 pages. Each request likely >32k? Maybe tool response 7*3k